  "final_message": "I put `channel` back everywhere I removed it, so `OrderPlaced` includes it again. I couldn't run the ARCH-4 check here, so the real confirmation is a fresh CI run.\n\nThe CI output shows `analytics-ingest` requires `OrderPlaced.channel` (enum `web|store|marketplace`), so my earlier claim that nothing reads it was wrong. The service can only fill the event field if the order model keeps `channel`, so I restored it in these places:\n- the `Order` and `NewOrder` types;\n- the `CHANNELS` list and its validation;\n- request parsing;\n- the event builder;\n- the tests and the README and CLAUDE.md examples.\n\n`npm test` passes (39/39) and `npm run typecheck` is clean. I did not rerun `npm run arch`.\n\nThe changes are uncommitted in the working tree. They are relative to the `gen` commit (`e361757`), which already contained the removal. I didn't create that commit, so I can't say who did.\n\nMy first attempt to restore the files with `git checkout` was blocked, so I undid the edits by hand. I fixed one slip from that, a dropped space in `order.ts`.\n\nIf `channel` should really go away, `analytics-ingest` has to stop requiring it first. That means changing its contract (not in this repo) and probably bumping the event `schemaVersion`. I can redo the removal after that.",
